% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Rx_PolElt_Ref -- the geometric TWIN of Rx_PolElt.in.
% PLAN_POLARIZATION Phase 3 (worklist item 4).
%
% Identical to Rx_PolElt.in except that elements 2/3/4/5 are plain Reference
% surfaces instead of TrPolarizer / WavePlate / WavePlate / TrPolarizer, and
% the PolAxis= / Retardance= keywords are absent.
%
% It exists to make ONE claim testable rather than argued: PolElt's geometry
% IS RefSrf's, so with polarization OFF a trace through the polarizing
% elements must be BIT-IDENTICAL to this file -- same ray status, same OPD,
% same spot, same intensity.  That is the "every non-polarized path stays
% bit-identical" requirement, and without this twin it would only ever be an
% inspection of the source.
%
% Keep the two files in sync: any geometric edit to Rx_PolElt.in belongs
% here too, or the gate silently starts comparing two different systems.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Source Definition
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

        ChfRayDir=  0.0E+00  0.0E+00  1.0E+00
        ChfRayPos=  0.0E+00  0.0E+00  -1.0E+00
          zSource=1.0E+21

        BaseUnits=  m
        WaveUnits=  m

           IndRef=1.0E+00
           Extinc=0.0E+00
          Wavelen=1.0E-06
             Flux=1.0E+00

         Aperture=1.0E-02
         Obscratn=0.0E+00

         GridType=  Circular
         nGridpts=  128
            xGrid=  1.0E+00  0.0E+00  0.0E+00
            yGrid=  0.0E+00  1.0E+00  0.0E+00

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Element Definitions
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

